25,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems our schedules are often delayed by weather and unexpected hazardous materials in the old walls.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found that general rooms are always full, while specialist ones are empty, and off-site hiring is expensive.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,George,,"Our technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks that equipment should handle, and we are short-staffed elsewhere.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Projects for comfort often slip by a year, and users prefer spaces that are open for general booking.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mechanical costs are rising sharply, and we have no reserve for replacing old audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that is worrying. It seems we are fighting both the market and the elements.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, so people really want more general-purpose spaces? That matches what I saw in the booking data.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, if we do more outdoor work, the weather and staffing gaps will only make it worse.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Exactly, Yumi. The data suggests that flexibility and accessibility are what the campus actually needs.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. We must be careful not to propose something that will bankrupt us or never be finished.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I worry about any plan that involves opening old walls or working outside in the winter.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Yumi,,But we really need more study space if the general rooms are always full!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,George,,I am more concerned about the technicians. They are exhausted by routines that are simply outdated.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,We should prioritize a project that is likely to be delivered on time and highly rated by users.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,A logical choice would avoid high-risk mechanical inflation unless it is absolutely necessary for safety.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Benjamin. Let us look for the most stable and helpful option.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I just want the students to have a place to study without us paying for off-site rentals.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,George,,"If the equipment is failing the staff, the ventilation upgrade seems urgent.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,We must weigh the staff's needs against the general student demand for space.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Let us see the candidates and apply these findings.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
